== GREEN 1: src/roots.c with Algorithm RR (adf_roots_real, real_finish, the hidden adf_roots_real_finish), the
   real place of the predicate and of the two verifiers, get_arb.
   First run: 7 tests ok, 1 failed check in predicate_at_the_real_place: a defect of the TEST. It expected the
   entries verifier to refuse the ball 1 +- 2^(1 - 2^24) for (X-1)(X-2)(X-3); that ball isolates the root 1 and
   passes the test of P3.8, so the entries verifier is right to accept it (the complete verifier refuses the list
   of one ball). The check now expects entries 1 and complete 0.
   The run took 92 s: 66 s in the planted test, (X - 10^400)(X - 10^400 - 1) at three precisions, 28 s each,
   all of it inside arb_fmpz_poly_complex_roots (measured alone: 28.3 s; its balls carry midpoints of 2^21 bits,
   accuracy 1456). That pair is now tested once, as a line of the vectors (it is a regression of
   check_s2_real_planted); X - 10^400 stays in the planted test.
   make -j2 build/test_roots_real && timeout 300 ./build/test_roots_real
   8 tests, 10666 checks, 0 failed checks, 0 failed tests; 30.6 s (28.9 s of them the vector line above)
   The prime tests, unchanged: test_roots_forged 2 tests, 26 checks, 0 failed. test_roots_seed 16 tests,
   5347209 checks, 1 failed (line 400); test_roots_padic 8 tests, 55131 checks, 1 failed (line 1237). Both
   failed checks assert the TEMPORARY 0 of slice 2 at the real place for the init list and f = 1, which is the
   true complete list of f = 1 (no real root): the header of slice 3 says 1. See result.md, and the proposed
   change lanes/s2-slice3/temporary-checks.patch (two lines, files not owned by this lane).

